asr-001934
01:35:24.301 --> 01:35:29.120
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: A regular DPWH program funded from the general appropriation, not from earmarked revenues

asr-001935
01:35:29.120 --> 01:35:32.500
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: So, we are talking about two different kinds of fund.

asr-001936
01:35:32.600 --> 01:35:38.820
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: One that is a statutorily earmarked special fund with appropriations under PD 1234.

asr-001937
01:35:39.100 --> 01:35:45.640
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: The other is an ordinary annual appropriation whose amount and scope are set by the DBM and by Congress each year.

asr-001938
01:35:45.640 --> 01:35:53.360
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: Under Republic Act 8794 as amended by RA 11239, the MVUC earmarked funds cover construction,

asr-001939
01:35:53.900 --> 01:35:57.260
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: upgrading, repair, and rehabilitation of roads, bridges, and road drainage.

asr-001940
01:35:58.600 --> 01:36:06.200
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: Under Fiscal Year 2027, the Asset Preservation covers preventive maintenance and rehabilitation of roads and drainage.

asr-001941
01:36:06.420 --> 01:36:10.580
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: But bridges are in a separate PAP, the bridge program.

asr-001942
01:36:10.580 --> 01:36:22.480
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: So, when the MVUC is subsumed inside Asset Preservation, part of the statutorily scope, the earmarked bridges, is no longer within the PAP.

asr-001943
01:36:22.480 --> 01:36:23.760
Rep. Isidro T. Ungab: That carries.

asr-001944
